goal:
  current: deliver the first runnable vertical slice (`CHG-003`) so `saaa evolve <folder>` runs one complete mutation evaluation end to end with no model credentials
  phase: implemented_on_branch

completed:
  - ran `.agentic-template/bin/project startup` and confirmed `AGENTS.md` from disk
  - read `HANDOFF.toon`, `PROJECT_PROFILE.toon`, `docs/context-store.md`, `.agents/knowledge/index.md`, `CON-001` and the `CHG-002` spec/design
  - added core value types `MutationOperatorType`, `FitnessObjective`, `MutationBounds`, `MutationTarget`, `SearchPosture`, `ParentTrait` and `MutationContract`
  - added application policies `MutationOperatorPolicy`, `MutationOperatorDefaults`, `MutationContractCanonicalizer`, `MutationContractValidator`, `PhenotypeFitnessScorer`, `PhenotypeEvidence`, `BehaviorCaseEvidence`, `ConceptualCrossoverPolicy` and `ConceptualCrossoverRequest`
  - extracted the shared authority-language regex from `BoundedMutationValidator` into `AuthorityLanguage` at its second use
  - made all six handed-over unit test classes pass without changing their assertions
  - obtained one independent actor review and fixed six of eight findings
  - added seven regression tests covering each applied review fix
  - recorded the two unfixed findings as `RISK-002`, `Q-007` and spec task `T4b`
  - updated `specs/changes/CHG-002-live-loop-policy/change.toon` task statuses and change status
  - merged the slice into `main` locally under the recorded PR-less fallback with explicit user authorization
  - renamed the package base from `io.github.selfadaptingagenticarchitecture` to `com.dreamthought.saaa`
  - moved all Java under `modules/` and renamed layers to `domain`, `deterministic`, `adapters`, `cli` and `benchmarks`
  - merged the four two-file adapter modules into one `modules/adapters` module
  - made `check-architecture-boundaries` fail loudly when a scanned layer directory is missing instead of passing vacuously
  - recorded the `invariant_named_module_layout` decision in `PROJECT_PROFILE.toon`
  - removed redundancy: renamed `SelfAdaptingAgenticArchitectureCli` to `MutationLoopCli`, pointed objective validation at the operator's own defaults instead of a duplicated constant, and dropped a duplicated enum assertion from the crossover test
  - implemented `CHG-003` Tasks 1-9 on branch `feat/first-vertical-slice`: `MutationRealizer` port and `TextMutationRealizer`, realization into the candidate commit, `RealizationInspector` port and `GitRealizationInspector`, `PhenotypeBridgeScorer` implementing `FitnessScorer`, `EvolutionReporter` port and loop reporting, fixture proposer and `ProposerProfileRegistry`, journal reporter and decision sink, toy-workflow fixture, and the `evolve` CLI command
  - fixed `GitRealizationInspector` to exclude `.saaa/` bookkeeping files from the candidate diff so parsimony measures only the real change
  - marked all `CHG-003` tasks complete and the change status `delivered`
  - recorded the `.saaa/fixture-mutation.txt` plain-text deviation in `docs/structured-data.md`
  - documented the `evolve` command in `README.md` and `docs/wiki/development.md`
  - found in lead review that `EvolveCommand` declared every `--behaviour-case` name to the scorer but wired only `behaviourCases.get(0)` into the check runner, so extra declared cases were never verified while the required-behaviour hard gate still reported pass
  - fixed it as `CHG-003` task `T8`: added `BehaviourCaseChecks` mapping each declared case to its own `<name>.sh`, rejecting unsafe names, absolute check directories and case-insensitive duplicates
  - obtained one independent actor review of the `T8` fix and fixed every finding it raised
  - fixed the actor-review blocker: a check directory that is empty because the target folder is the Git root produced a command with no path separator, which execvp resolves against `PATH` rather than the candidate worktree, so a script outside the candidate could satisfy a required behaviour
  - made the command refuse to run unless every declared case has an executable script, so a typo or missing script is never recorded as evidence about the mutation
  - made `PhenotypeBridgeScorer` fail the behaviour gate closed when a declared case produced no evidence, moving the invariant into the layer that owns the gate instead of relying on the CLI wiring it correctly
  - anchored the `GitRealizationInspector` pathspecs at the repository root with `:/` and `(top,exclude)` so the measurement no longer depends on the caller's working directory
  - recorded `RISK-003` for candidate worktree name collisions across runs
  - recorded `CHG-003` tasks `T9` and `T10` for the deferred reporter-diagnostics and non-empty-realization gate findings

in_progress:
  - `CHG-003` branch `feat/first-vertical-slice` is implemented, reviewed and committed but not yet merged to `main`

next:
  - merge `feat/first-vertical-slice` to `main` under the PR-less fallback (requires explicit user authorization) or after `gh` token scope is granted
  - implement `T9` so a failed behaviour case shows why it failed, and `T10` so a no-op realization cannot be promoted
  - grant the `gh` token pull-request scope so future slices use a PR instead of the recorded fallback
  - implement `T4b` so declared contract hard gates are enforced by the scorer, not only declared
  - implement `T3d` TOON mutation contract envelope parser feeding the canonicalizer
  - migrate `MutationEvaluationLoop` from the transitional `Mutation`/`MutationValidator`/`FitnessScorer` stack onto `MutationContract` and `PhenotypeFitnessScorer`; both stacks exist today, only the old one is wired
  - implement `CHG-002` `T2`, `T5`, `T6` before any live provider run
  - the population slice: evaluate several candidates per generation and rank them, calling `MutationEvaluationLoop.evaluate` N times

decisions:
  - id: langchain4j_adapter_boundary
    summary: LangChain4j stays in the `adapters/langchain4j` package of `modules/adapters`; `modules/domain` and `modules/deterministic` stay provider-free
  - id: deterministic_approval_boundary
    summary: model output may propose or repair but validation, scoring, promotion and rollback are deterministic
  - id: mutation_contract_ir_policy
    summary: TOON is the reviewable mutation-contract envelope; canonical S-expression is the internal mutation/operator IR; Git diffs are candidate realization evidence
  - id: closed_operator_enum
    summary: ten closed operator values; `conceptual-crossover` is deliberately absent and negatively tested
  - id: conceptual_crossover_boundary
    summary: conceptual crossover is a recombination policy producing a bounded child mutation contract; the policy now validates its own child before emitting it
  - id: phenotype_fitness_policy
    summary: hard gates run before weighted objectives and are not tradeable; promotion threshold is `0.80` compared against the raw sum, with rounding applied to the reported score only
  - id: canonical_ir_safety
    summary: unquoted IR positions are checked against a safe atom/identifier shape so model-authored text cannot forge nodes such as an extra gate
  - id: gate_outcomes_win_in_audit_record
    summary: gate outcomes are written after measured scores in `FitnessResult.objectives` so evidence content cannot overwrite a recorded gate result

risks:
  - RISK-002: the scorer enforces its own fixed gates and never sees the contract, so a declared `required_evidence_present` gate can pass without the evidence it names; tracked as `T4b`
  - Q-007: canonical IR preserves declared order for set-like fields, so contracts differing only in evidence order canonicalize differently
  - the new `MutationContract` / `MutationContractValidator` / `PhenotypeFitnessScorer` stack is parallel to the wired `Mutation` / `MutationValidator` / `FitnessScorer` ports and is reachable only from tests; the design records `Mutation.patch` as transitional but no migration step is scheduled yet
  - `PhenotypeFitnessScorer` does not implement the `FitnessScorer` port, so `MutationEvaluationLoop` cannot use it until the contract is threaded through
  - benchmark presence is not yet a hard gate because "required benchmark evidence" is contract-dependent and the scorer has no contract input
  - direct main shipping still requires branch isolation, deterministic checks, actor review or recorded fallback, lead self-review and explicit user authorization
  - the fixture proposer is deterministic by design, so it cannot demonstrate that a real model produces useful mutations; it only proves the pipe
  - `behavioral_safety` has no independent evidence source in this slice and is fixed at 1.0, leaving one of five objectives inert
  - `journal.md` is written into the user's target folder, so the command writes outside its own repository
  - the `.saaa` pathspec exclusion in `GitRealizationInspector` is coupled by convention to `GitCandidateWorkspace`, which writes bookkeeping under `.saaa/candidates/`; a future adapter writing bookkeeping elsewhere would need the exclusion updated
  - `ExperimentMetadataStore` is a no-op in the CLI wiring; persistent experiment metadata arrives with `CHG-002` task `T5`
  - `CHG-003` branch is implemented, reviewed and committed but not yet merged to `main`
  - RISK-003: candidate worktree names derive only from workflow and mutation ids, so a repeat run of the same mutation against one folder fails until `.worktrees/candidate-*` is removed; blocking at the population slice
  - reporters print only check name and status, so a behaviour case that fails for its own reasons shows no diagnostics; tracked as `CHG-003` task `T9`
  - no gate requires a non-empty realization, so a candidate that changed nothing scores parsimony 1.0; tracked as `CHG-003` task `T10`
  - behaviour case names double as script file names, so a case name is constrained to `[a-zA-Z0-9][a-zA-Z0-9._-]*` and the per-case check timeout is fixed at one minute
  - check scripts run in a worktree created from `HEAD`, so a new check script must be committed before it can gate a run

